purpose: Who names branches, and what does the branch model define instead?

Records the decision that the vcs-gov branch model defines only roles and promotion direction, while the project declares branch names and prefixes in vcs.branch.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; decisions, date, check list items and the ADR 0017 supersession note are unchanged.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
All identifiers (required-roles, branch-defaults, engsys vcs base-branch, check-settings, init --detect, public-ai-qa) kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.
Checked against the HEAD Korean text for dropped facts: the local-rule constraint on server protected branches appears in both Context and Consequences as in the source.

